(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-painting-decision :authorize-coating-application :proceed-with-painting-work :override-site-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage" "2799007121-cloud-itonami-isco-7121-roofers-coverage" "2799009311-cloud-itonami-isco-9311-mining-quarrying-labourers-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the painting work" "finalize the painting decision" "authorize the coating application" "authorize the paint application" "override the site safety officer's judgment" "override site safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007131), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :construction/painting-site-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :painter-verified :site-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7131"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007131: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7131 Painters and Related Workers job-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7131\n-- Painters and Related Workers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of\nthe rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batch1 of 6 already landed:\n7111/7112/7113/7114/7119/7121).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7131\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (pr-str (kotoba.occupation/\nget-occupation \\\"7131\\\")))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Painters and Related Workers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7131` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7131` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nPainters apply coatings/finishes on active job sites -- real\nphysical-safety stakes (solvent/fume exposure, height-work for\nexteriors, ventilation requirements). The controlling constraint for\nthis vertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any\nop that directly finalizes a painting-execution decision, or overrides\na site safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a\nhard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to JOB-SITE\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs painting\nwork itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave/domain shape,\njust landed) -- cloned and read in full in this session. The\nphysical-safety-domain shape (closed allowlist + always-escalate\nsafety flag + content-based scope-exclusion with a self-trip\nregression test) was cross-checked against\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9311`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9311)\n(Mining and Quarrying Labourers) -- also cloned and read in full.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7131` as an OSS job-site\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for painters, following the\nSAME governed-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Paint Crew Advisor ⊣ PaintCrewGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **job-site scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct painting-execution authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\npainting-execution decision, or any override of a site safety\nofficer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a fume-exposure/ventilation/\n  height-work concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- paint/coating-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\npainting-execution decision or a site-safety-officer-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-painting-decision` cannot even be proposed by the reference\nmock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one\nof the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a\nfuture LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the\ngovernor's closed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it\nunconditionally and permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names four concretely-forbidden ops\n(`paintcrew.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-painting-decision`, `:authorize-coating-application`,\n`:proceed-with-painting-work`, `:override-site-safety-officer-judgment`)\nas defense-in-depth, and is verified by dedicated unit tests\n(`paintcrew.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-painting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-coating-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-painting-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-site-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Painter unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered painter record (`:no-painter`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the painter is.\n2. **Site unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered job site (`:no-site`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a worker/site\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any\n   action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the four\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with painting\n   work, or overriding a site safety officer's judgment, is a second\n   HARD, PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   painting-execution/safety-override language wherever it appears in\n   free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a fume-exposure/\n  ventilation/height-work observation -- it never resolves the concern\n  itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard data,\"\n  never \"here is what I recommend doing about site safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  paint/coating-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  painting-execution or safety-officer-override attempt, which is why\n  it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural\n  absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"paint\", \"coating\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a job-site coordination actor working\nadjacent to coating/painting work necessarily discusses those concepts\nto do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`paintcrew.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the painting work\",\n\"authorize the coating application\", \"override the site safety\nofficer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`paintcrew.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for painter ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for coating\ntask ...\", \"... routed for site safety officer review\") WITHOUT\ncontaining any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development. `paintcrew.actor-test/holds-a-scope-\nexcluded-op-even-at-high-confidence` additionally exercises the same\ninvariant through the full graph run, confirming a scope-excluded\nproposal never reaches `commit-record!` regardless of disposition\npath.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7131\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7131` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7131`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-coating-application` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  painting-execution decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (solvent/fume\n  exposure, falls from height, ventilation hazards), the capability\n  itself must not exist. The only op related to site-safety escalation\n  is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/site-\n  safety-officer attention and never itself decides, authorizes, or\n  defers a painting-execution decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold paint/\n  coating-materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a\n  soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the painting-execution/\n  safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"paint\" \"coating\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses paint/\n  coating/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so\n  a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- A second override-authority op mirroring house-building's dual\n  safety-officer/foreman split (`:override-safety-officer-judgment`\n  AND `:override-foreman-judgment`): rejected -- the task's domain\n  design names only \"a site-safety officer's judgment\" as the\n  authority figure for this vertical, so a single\n  `:override-site-safety-officer-judgment` op (plus matching phrase\n  variants) fully covers the specified scope without inventing an\n  unspecified second authority role.\n- Merging `painter` and `site` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered painter AND independently-registered site)\n  matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/site record must be\n  independently verified/registered before any action\" and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered painter AND\n   site (`:no-painter`/`:no-site`). Not a painting-execution or\n   safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a painting-execution decision (structurally\n   absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt via free text is\n   caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not\n   authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific\n   coating or finish application -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a fume-exposure/ventilation/\n   height-work concern to a human/site safety officer; ALWAYS\n   escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the site safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- paint/coating-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a painting-execution or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na painting-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific coating\nor finish application) or a site-safety-officer-judgment override --\nthese categories are structurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a)\nthe closed four-op allowlist itself (`paintcrew.governor/allowed-ops`),\n(b) four concretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the\ngovernor-unit level (`paintcrew.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`paintcrew.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-painting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-coating-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-painting-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-site-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`paintcrew.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with painting work or override a site safety\nofficer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`paintcrew.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-site-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Painting Site Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :painter-verification :site-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7131"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7131"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7131)), (:test/simulator :paintcrew.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7131 — Painters and Related Workers Job-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7131)))